00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:00.870 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  universal's 1999 remake of the mummy was  a cultural reset for both the property  and hollywood as a whole it arguably  changed action movies helping usher in  the era of cgi villains and heavily  comedic heroes one of those heroes  rachel vice's evelyn carnahan propels  the action of the first mummy film she  is the one who recognizes the  significance of the puzzle box that  leads them to the city of hamanopdra she  reads the incantation that awakens emote  and it is her soul that the undead  priest wants to give to his dearly  departed girlfriend evelyn is a huge  part of the mummy franchise's appeal  fans love the movie's blend of action  romance and comedy all of which vice  contributes to she channels screwball  comediennes of the 30s for her sparkling  performance the stranger noted in its  review how perfect she was to play  evelyn saying she has all the spunk and  ditzy charm you'd expect from a heroine  who can proudly proclaim she's not just  smart she's a librarian for goodness  sake  let's be nice children  the mummy series arguably fell off when  vice failed to return for the mummy tomb  of the dragon emperor the third  installment in the mummy series a  representative of ice told digital spy  that she didn't want to go to china and  spend so much time away from her at the  time newborn son after leaving the mummy  franchise vice went on to work steadily  in movies both big and small but her  most critically acclaimed work of late  has been on a much smaller scale than  the mummy rachel vice won an academy  award not long after the mummy returns  for her performance in the 2005  adaptation of john lichterrez the  constant gardener the film centers on  rafe finds justin quail who tries to  solve the murder of his wife vice plays  the ill-fated wife tessa an amnesty  activist in kenya vice also has had some  brief dalliances with other blockbuster  franchises post mummy the same year she  starred in the constant gardner she made  a foray into comic book adaptations with  the cult favorite constantine she'd go  on to star in the bourne legacy opposite  jeremy renner before doing her time in  the mcu playing melina vostikov in black  widow in 2021 vostikov is something of a  mother figure to scarlett johansson's  natasha romanov and florence pugh's  yelina bilova as of yet there's been no  word if bosticoff will return to the mcu  but there's little doubt fans would  adore seeing her again while vice's  experience with blockbusters is  extensive her most notable work of late  has been in more indie fair vice first  worked with greek director jorgos  lantimos on his 2015 black comedy the  lobster she played a woman searching for  love before she gets turned into an  animal she would reunite with lantimos  for 2018's the favorite in which she  plays lady sarah churchill lady sarah  starts the film as the titular favorite  of queen anne played by olivia coleman  as well as her secret girlfriend emma  stone plays abigail who woos the queen  away from lady sarah in an attempt to  stay in power in court coleman won an  academy award for her performance as  queen f the apex of the unlikely love  triangle while stone and vice were both  nominated for best supporting actress  the same year as the favorite vice  starred in disobedience opposite rachel  mcadams the drama focuses on two women  from the orthodox jewish community who  try to reconcile their love for each  other with their sometimes overbearingly  strict community  despite being married to a man daniel  cred aka james bond vice's performances  in these films have vault advice into  queer icon status in the lgbtq community  vice's queer turn may have something to  do with the fact that she's primarily  focused on women-centered stories she  told the new york times i really enjoy  all the thousands of movies i've seen  about men i mean there are some great  masterpieces but there's just a darth of  ones about women i love women women are  just really fascinating and different to  men fans can likely expect this trend to  continue with vice's future projects  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite actors are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

